## How it's graded

This Canvas entry only records that the plan was turned in. The plan's quality is graded once, as the **MVP plan quality** criterion of CP10 (15 of its 100 points; CP10 = 16% of the course). **The revision you submit end of day {{ S20_DAY }} is the version scored;** the score is recorded with CP10 on {{ S22_DATE }}. Later amendments don't change this score; they change what the demo is judged against (see *Submission*).

| Level | What it looks like |
|---|---|
| **Exemplary (4)** | In and deferred both named, throwaway corners labeled; the risk tied to its evidence; ranked claims, a falsifier, a three-line script, and a real fallback |
| **Proficient (3)** | All four parts present and clear; the claims or the fallback a little thin |
| **Developing (2)** | Features listed without claims, or nothing honestly deferred, or no fallback |
| **Beginning (1)** | Missing, or a wish list |

The rest of CP10 (the demo itself, the slice, the audit) is graded {{ S22_DATE }}: see <course-link type="assignment" id="cp10">CP10 — Progress Demo + Repo Audit</course-link>.

